MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Coup Attempt
  crisisName: Coup Attempt
  ominousWarningText: "Officers have begun whispering behind closed doors. Senior military and political figures hold meetings outside normal channels, while private messages move between commanders who rarely dealt with one another before. Loyal officials report that routine orders are being questioned or delayed, and several units have unexpectedly changed commanders without clear authorization. Rumors circulate through the capital of secret pledges, lists of political enemies, and promises of promotion once the current leadership is gone. No one is willing to accuse the conspirators openly without proof, and many powerful figures remain carefully silent. The government still commands the army on paper. It is becoming less clear who the army will obey when that authority is tested."
  obviousWarningText: "Loyal troops report unauthorized military movements across the capital. Units have taken positions near government buildings, communications centers, armories, and major roads without orders from civilian authorities. Several senior officers have stopped answering official messages, while competing commands circulate contradictory instructions through the armed forces. Government guards seal entrances as ministers attempt to determine which commanders can still be trusted. Rumors of arrests and defections race through the city faster than they can be confirmed. The conspiracy has moved beyond private meetings and whispered promises. Someone is making their move."
  crisisStartText: "The conspiracy has become an open struggle for control of the state. Disloyal officers and their allies are moving against the government, attempting to seize the capital, secure military installations, and bring wavering commanders to their side. Governors, factions, and units whose loyalty is uncertain may now become active participants in the crisis, while the government must determine whom it can still trust. The coup can be confronted through force, political concessions, or an attempt to dismantle the conspiracy before it captures the machinery of government. Losing the capital or allowing the rebels to consolidate their position could transform a conspiracy into a new regime. Authority now depends on more than laws—it depends on who obeys them."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 12
